{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"![image.png](attachment:adb98fe5-2684-49ba-a488-a0080af365ab.png)","metadata":{},"attachments":{"adb98fe5-2684-49ba-a488-a0080af365ab.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"![image.png](attachment:24d933bf-b748-4cb2-b81f-c09edcc5f8a8.png)","metadata":{},"attachments":{"24d933bf-b748-4cb2-b81f-c09edcc5f8a8.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Machine Learning\n\n![image.png](attachment:52f93d6c-67a3-41b3-bebd-44c3296559d1.png)\n\n![image.png](attachment:58ec50b3-976f-4eb4-97e7-7a9e65399c24.png)","metadata":{},"attachments":{"52f93d6c-67a3-41b3-bebd-44c3296559d1.png":{"image/png":""},"58ec50b3-976f-4eb4-97e7-7a9e65399c24.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Types of machine learning Models:\n1. Discriminative Models\n2. Generative Models","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Based on Learning: (Discriminative)\n1. Spupervised learning\n2. Un-Supervised learning\n3. Reinforcement learning","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Spuervised learning\n\nSupervised learning is a type of machine learning where a model learns from labeled data. This means the input data already has the correct output or answer.\n\n2 types of SL:\n\n1. Classification tasks\n2. Regression tasks","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Classification Tasks\n\nClassification means predicting a **category or class**.\n\n### Example\n\n![Apple Classification Example](attachment:c5fd2a2a-da45-4a83-9984-6e0ebf5ef199.png)\n\nFor example, suppose we want to classify different types of fruits:\n\n- **Input:** Fruit image → **Apple**\n- **Input:** Fruit image → **Orange**\n- **Input:** Fruit image → **Banana**\n\nThe model's output is a **class/category**, not a numerical value.\n\n### Other Examples\n\n- **Cancer** → Benign / Malignant\n- **Email** → Spam / Not Spam\n- **Fruit** → Apple / Orange / Banana","metadata":{},"attachments":{"c5fd2a2a-da45-4a83-9984-6e0ebf5ef199.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Regression Tasks\n\nRegression means predicting a **continuous numerical value**.\n\n### Example\n\n![Regression Example](attachment:83cfe86d-9d9c-4847-a633-fcdb667bb991.png)\n\nSuppose we have an apple with the following features:\n\n- **Weight:** 150g\n- **Size:** Medium\n- **Color:** Red\n\nThe model predicts:\n\n**Price = $2.50**\n\nHere, **$2.50** is a continuous numerical value, so this is a **regression task**.\n\n### Other Examples\n\n- **House features** → House price\n- **Temperature data** → Tomorrow's temperature\n- **Car features** → Car price\n- **Student study hours** → Exam score","metadata":{},"attachments":{"83cfe86d-9d9c-4847-a633-fcdb667bb991.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Unsupervised learning\n\nUnsupervised learning is a type of machine learning where the model learns from **unlabeled data**.\nThis means we give the model data, but we do not provide the correct output or class labels. The model tries to discover patterns, structures, or groups in the data by itself.\n\n**2 types of UL:**\n1. Clustering\n2. Dimension Reduction\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"![Screenshot 2026-08-15 101442.png](attachment:63567ddd-6958-40ae-bbd2-4ae8b13d3866.png)","metadata":{},"attachments":{"63567ddd-6958-40ae-bbd2-4ae8b13d3866.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Clustering\n\nClustering means grouping similar data points together **without predefined labels**.\n\n### Example\n\nSuppose we give the model many fruit images, but we don't tell it which one is **Apple, Orange, or Banana**.\n\nThe model looks at features such as **color, shape, size, and texture** and creates groups:\n\n- **Group 1** → Similar-looking fruits\n- **Group 2** → Similar-looking fruits\n- **Group 3** → Similar-looking fruits\n\nThe model creates these groups **by itself**.\n\n### Example Algorithm\n\n- **K-Means Clustering**\n\n> **Clustering = Find similar groups in unlabeled data.**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Dimensionality Reduction\n\nDimensionality reduction means reducing the **number of features/dimensions** in a dataset while trying to preserve the most important information.\n\n### Example\n\nSuppose each image has **1,000 features**.\n\nInstead of working with all 1,000 features, we can reduce them to:\n\n**1,000 features → 2 features**\n\nNow, we can visualize the data in a **2D graph** while still preserving much of the important structure.\n\n### Common Algorithms\n\n- **PCA (Principal Component Analysis)**\n- **t-SNE**\n- **UMAP**\n\n> **Dimensionality Reduction = Reduce features while preserving important information.**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**The main difference between SL & USL is label and unlabel data.** \n\n![image.png](attachment:48db25b6-d393-40f8-9951-69ac40ac35ba.png)","metadata":{},"attachments":{"48db25b6-d393-40f8-9951-69ac40ac35ba.png":{"image/png":""}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Generative Model\n\nA **Generative Model** is a type of machine learning model that learns the **patterns and distribution of existing data** and then generates **new data similar to the training data**.\n\n### Examples\n\n- **Text** → ChatGPT\n- **Images** → DALL·E, Midjourney\n- **Video** → Sora\n- **Music/Audio** → Suno\n- **Speech** → Voice generation\n- **Code** → GitHub Copilot\n- **3D Models** → 3D generation\n- **Synthetic Data** → Artificial datasets\n- **Molecules** → Drug discovery\n- **Medical Images** → X-ray, MRI, histopathology images","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# LLM \n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":" ","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null}]}